It is recommended that:  
1. The Australian Consumer Law be amended to  make the individual/s controlling 
a legal person  personally accountable for its AI use.  
 
A suggestion for a new section to be inserted in the Australian Consumer Law is: 
 
Accessory li ability for contravention  arising through use of a rtificial 
intelligence  tool 
Where conduct that contraven es a provision of this Schedule is caused by the use 
of an artificial intelligence tool, then the following individuals  are liable as 
accessories for that con travention :  
(i) If a corporation  or a listed corporation used the artificial 
intelligence tool, t he officers  of that corporation  or listed corporation 
are jointly and severally liable  as accessories ; and 
(ii) If a partnership used the artificial intelligence tool, the  partners of 
a partnership are jointly and severally liable  as accessories . 
 
 
2. The Privacy Act 1988  be amended to make the individual/s controlling an 
organisation  personally accountable for that organisation ’s AI use.   
A suggestion for a new section is : 
Accessory liability  for breach arising through use of artificial intelligence  
tool  
If an organisation is liable for a breach6 arising out of the  use of an artificial 
intelligence tool , then the following persons are liable as accessories for that 
breach : 
a) The officers  of a corporation are jointly and severally liable as 
accessories  for that breach ;  
b) The executive  and elected  officers , howsoever called,  of a n 
unincorporated  association are jointly and severally liable for that breach ; 
and 
c) If the trustee of a trust is a corporation, the officers  of the trustee  
corporation  are jointly and severally liable for that breach . 
For the avoidance of doubt, the  partners of a partnership are jointly and 
severally liable for any breach . 
 
  
 
