include a legally binding right to receive a personal explanation of a high -risk AI/automated  
decision, to know when you are interacting with AI -generated or augmented material and 
to be informed when you are party to an automated decision -making process.  
 
4.7 Guardrail 7: Contestability  
 
Imagine waking up every day knowing that your livelihood is dictated by a … cold, 
unfeeling piece of code that determines whether you get work , how much you’re 
paid and whether you’ll still have a job. There’s no transparency, no negotiation, just 
a digital overload that issues commands we must obey…. If we’re delayed by traffic, 
the algorithm … threaten[s] to deactivate us if we don’t speed up… the algorithm 
decides our fate  – no questions asked, no context considered . 
Ustav Bhattarai, Rideshare Driver and Health and Safety Representative , TWU .77 
 
Guardrail 7 deals with one of the most important topics of AI regulation but  unfortunately 
contains the least detail. Contestability refers to the ability of Australians to meaningfully 
challenge automated decisions that impact them. Automated decision making opens  a 
 
