Recommendation 19: Ensure there is a strong enforcement mechanism  with a 
designated AI regulator  
An AI regulator with broad powers must be given a  mandate to redesign of AI systems, 
collect information about  their function and ensure accountability for those  failing to 
comply with  the AI guardrails. Compliance should not be automatically assumed and 
unsupervised conformity assessments should be replaced by a pre -deployment approval 
process undertaken by the regulator.  
 
Recommendation 2 0: Legislate penalties for failing to comply with  the AI guardrails  
Ensure the regulator is able to  enforce penalties for violations of the guardrails , the  Charter 
or any other component of the AI regulatory  framework. Penalties should be sufficient  to 
act as a deterrent. Penalties should be calculated with due consideration of:  
i. The nature, gravity, scale and intensity of harm resulting from the infringement ; 
ii. The size, annual turnover and market power of the offender ; 
iii. The manner in which the infringement became known ; 
iv. Any financial benefits gained, or financial losses avoided, including indirectly, 
from the infringement ; 
v. Any industrial relations benefits gained for the offender related to the 
infringement ; 
vi. The offenders’ degree of co -operation with supervisory authorities, public 
interest organisations, and registered employee organisations ; and  
vii. The intentional or negligent character of the infringement.  
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
    
 
