4 October 2024  
 
Re: Proposed mandatory guardrails for high -risk AI in Australia  
 
The Department of Industry, Science and Resources’ recent proposals paper for 
introducing mandatory guardrails for AI in high -risk settings1 is a major step towards 
introducing clear and transparent AI regulation in Australia – so organisations can 
confidently innovate and scale with AI, benefitting both our economy and society. The faster 
the Australian Government accelerates this proces s, the sooner  Australia will be able to 
keep pace with and compete with confidence on the global AI stage.  
 
This submission builds on our previous submission2 which focused on how Australian 
organisations can harness AI’s potential in a safe and responsible way. As before, our views 
are built on global and local consultation with Deloitte experts across technology, 
regulations, risk management and governance – as well as our own deep understanding of 
the challenges our clients face in developing best practice AI solutions.  
 
Time is of the essence. We must have clear definitions and effective rules and regulations in 
place as soon as possible, so more organisations can safely, responsibly, and quickly adopt 
AI with clarity on regulatory settings and drive Australia onto the gl obal stage.  
  
 
1 Australian Government,  ‘Introducing Mandatory Guardrails for AI in High -Risk Settings: Proposals Paper ’ 
(2024)  https://consult.industry.gov.au/ai -mandatory -guardrails . 
