International alignment and harmonisation  
The challenge of ensuring safe and effective adoption and integration of AI and its associated 
capabilities is not unique to Australia. Around the world, governments are moving to introduce 
appropriate legislation and regulations to simultaneously manage risks and leverage opportunities 
associated with AI capability. The TGA recognises the importance of maintaining international 
harmonisation in terms of regulatory approaches towards therapeutic goods in order to facilitate access to imported emerging technology by Australian consumers and healthcare professionals, and 
to support export of products manufactured domestically.  
Our proposals therefore:  Therapeutic Goods Administration  
 
