sensitivities, especially regarding the use of Indigenous data and imagery. Culturally 
informed data governance standards should be established, ensuring that data collected 
or used for AI development respects Indigenous Data Sovereignty, ICIP, and existin g 
cultural practices. This includes ensuring that data storage, access, and use follow 
cultural protocols, particularly around sacred knowledge that should not be used or 
shared without explicit community consent. Additionally, there should be ongoing 
monitoring and accountability mechanisms to ensure AI systems remain aligned with 
First Nations cultural protocols throughout their lifecycle. These mechanisms must 
include provisions for dispute resolution and legal recourse for Indigenous communities 
