Professional accountants  
Our members  are held accountable to CA ANZ’s, Australian and international professional 
standards  for the use of AI, not only high -risk AI systems . The relevant Standards are 
captured in the Code of Ethics for Professional Accountants ( APES 110 ) and the 
accommodation of technology -related revisions to the International Code of Ethics for 
Professional Accountants . 
These recognise that the risks are significant and serious if both the inputs and outputs of AI 
are either not used appropriately or not critically evaluated. Furthermore, as our members  
are using data inputs which are owned by third parties, confidentiality and privacy must be 
appropriately managed in accordance with APES 110  and relevant laws and regulations  
Broadly, as relevan t to AI, members need to understand what a tool utilising AI is doing and 
not claim work that is  not their own.    © Chartered Accountants Australia and New Zealand  
