6. Should mandatory guardrails apply to all GPAI models?
No
Please provide any additional comments.
Mandatory guardrails should be carefully targeted at regulating the most high risk models that pose a catastrophic or existential threat. It would be bad to have an approach that stifles the benefits of advances in AI, while being ineffective at preventing worst case scenarios.
11. Are the proposed mandatory guardrails sufficient to address the risks of GPAI?
No
How could we adapt the guardrails for different GPAI models, for example low-risk and high-risk GPAI models? 
The greatest focus should be given to the greatest potential for harm. It is very difficult to know at this stage how we can best mitigate the risk of the future models that have this potential and where we might draw the ‘red lines’ that could trigger stringent regulatory responses. Nonetheless, these considerations should be the primary goal of mandatory guardrails.
13. Which legislative option do you feel will best address the use of AI in high-risk settings?
A whole of economy approach – introducing a new cross-economy AI Act
What opportunities should the Government take into account in considering each approach? 
A whole of economy approach involving an Australian AI Act is highly desirable since only a new, targeted and well designed regulator would have the agility and expertise needed to respond against the rapid speed at which advances in AI are increasingly taking place.
15. Which regulatory option(s) will best ensure that guardrails for high-risk AI can adapt and respond to step-changes in technology?
A whole of economy approach – introducing a new cross-economy AI Act
Make a general comment
As a recent graduate of computer science, I am both excited about and alarmed by the incredible pace at which AI has been developing. Unfortunately however, I am sceptical of our ultimate ability to control AI as it gets closer to parity with human intelligence.
I am heartened that the Australian Government is taking the threat seriously. I hope that in our continuing efforts as a country, we pay close attention to the most outsized negative impacts.

