Introduction
While disruption is on the horizon, so is opportunity.When generative AI (GenAI) burst into 
public consciousness after the November 
2022 launch of ChatGPT, it sent shock 
waves through every corner of the 
business world. Leaders wondered what 
it would mean for their workforce, and 
employees worried their jobs would be 
taken away. Today, some of the dust has 
settled and more data is in. The headline: 
While disruption is on the horizon, so 
is opportunity.
 
Our Impact AI: 2024 Workforce Skills 
Forecast  applies advanced AI modeling 
to workforce data from eight major 
economies worldwide. We set out to 
understand which jobs will be impacted 
by AI, which skills will be automated, 
which roles will be in highest demand, and 
how leaders can reskill their workforce 
to future-proof their businesses. Here’s 
what we learned about how to prepare 
your organization—and yourself—for the 
seismic impact that GenAI and related 
technologies will have on the workplace. AI Impact: 2024 Workforce Skills Forecast4For the second year in a row, ServiceNow 
partnered with workforce data experts Pearson 
to model the impact of GenAI and related 
technologies on the global workforce. Pearson 
data scientists built machine learning algorithms 
that combed census data, job boards, and other 
labor market data troves. We mined that data to 
predict how AI will change the mix of skills required 
to perform thousands of different jobs over the 
next five years. Our research looked at 1,400 occupations and 
broke them into 5,600 job functions made of 
80,000 tasks. The analysis covers Australia, 
Canada, Germany, India, Japan, Singapore, the 
UK, and the United States, making this one of the 
world’s most comprehensive studies of how AI will 
impact the global workforce.Methodology
