markets such as India, where we predict demand for  an 
additional 34 million workers to sustain an estimated 
annual growth rate of 6.3% over the next five years. 
Second is the United States, where an additional 1 million 
workers will be needed to support predicted annual GDP 
growth of 2.1%. 
Even considering jobs that will be automated away and 
the tasks that will be made more efficient by the use of AI, 
we are still going to experience a global labor shortage. 
In fact, the productivity gains we will achieve because of 
emerging technologies are  the main reason this worker 
deficit won’t be more extreme. 
