14To achieve this optimistic vision—and 
to support healthy economic growth—
businesses and governments must 
provide training opportunities that 
position workers for success amid rising 
automation. This can only be done by 
understanding which skills are on the 
wane and which are on the rise in the 
IT industry and beyond. 
For example, we know the work of 
account management specialists will 
be heavily impacted by automation 
in coming years. However, today’s 
account managers have numerous 
professional skills that translate to 
occupations that will be in higher 
demand. We mapped the transferable 
skills between account management 
specialist and technical project 
manager, a role we know will grow 
in demand. It turns out that account 
management specialists already 
have or are close to having 80% of 
the skills needed to transition to 
technical project manager. With some 
strategic reskilling, they can easily 
make the transition to a new, more in-
demand position.
