India
The Indian workforce is poised for massive growth. 
The IMF estimates that the Indian economy will grow 
at an annual rate of 6.3% over the next five years. 
Without taking the productivity-boosting effects of AI 
into account, the Indian economy would need to add 
47 .57 million people to the workforce over five years to 
support this growth rate. Our research predicts that AI 
will be able to do the work equivalent to 16.41 million 
full-time employees. To realize this potential, however, 
an additional 2.73 million tech jobs will be needed to 
implement and maintain emerging technologies. 
When all factors are considered, 
the Indian economy will need 
an additional 34 million workers 
by 2028. 
The short story is that AI, like many technologies before 
it, will disrupt the workforce while creating net-positive 
job gain. To benefit from these shifts, Indian workers must 
acquire skills that are relevant in a technology-centric 
work environment.AI Impact: 2024 Workforce Skills Forecast
