skills trends:  
Japan
Japan’s workforce will see an overall decline over the 
next five years, likely due to an aging population. 
The Bank of Japan (BOJ) estimates that the Japanese 
economy will grow at an annual rate of 1.0% over the 
next five years. Without taking the productivity-boosting 
effects of AI into account, the Japanese economy would 
need to add 2.25 million people to the workforce over 
five years to support this growth rate. Our research 
predicts that AI will be able to do the work equivalent to 
4.56 million full-time employees. To realize this potential, 
however, an additional .41 million tech jobs will be needed 
to implement and maintain emerging technologies. 
When all factors are considered, 
the Japanese economy will 
see a -1.55 million decrease in 
workforce by 2028. 
To account for the reduced workforce, Japanese business 
leaders will need to invest in innovative recruitment and 
training strategies.AI Impact: 2024 Workforce Skills Forecast
