Audit
Criteria
6.1
Definitions
Defined
terms
(bolded
and
capitalised)
are
used,
like
in
contract
law,
to
make
the
interpretation
easier
and
to
reduce
ambiguity.
They
are
purposefully
defined
to
incorporate
key
concepts
and
often
aspects
of
law
that
are
required
for
compliance.
The
certification
scheme
is
built
on
the
foundation
of
a
common
lexicon.
When
globally
recognised
standards
bodies
have
provided
a
suitable
definition,
ForHumanity
will
adopt
it.
When
the
law
defines
the
term,
ForHumanity
will
use
the
legal
definition.
6.2
Protected
Categories
When
a
jurisdiction
takes
legal
steps
to
protect
certain
groups
of
people
or
aspects
of
a
person’s
innate
characteristics,
from
discrimination
and/or
bias,
the
audit
describes
these
aspects
or
classes
as
Protected
Categories
and
exist
in
varied
forms
such
as
Protected
Categories,
Protected
Variables,
and
Proxy
Variables.
The
use
of
Protected
Category
variables
indicates
that
the
associated
data
process
or
AAA
System
must
go
through
bias
remediation.
Further,
the
use
of
Protected
Category
variables
may
also
indicate
the
need
for
Special
data
process
rules
such
as
further
lawful
basis
assurance
or
a
higher
degree
of
cybersecurity.
