environmental consequences, including pollution, deforestation, and habitat destruction (Roberts, 2008). 
Ethical Concerns:  The development of new technologies raised ethical concerns, such as privacy, surveillance, and 
the responsible use of scientific advancements (Miller, 2013). 
As we continue to navigate the challenges and opportunities of the modern age, the lessons of the Scientific-
Technical Revolution serve as a reminder of the importance of balancing progress with ethical and social 
considerations. 
